join Mallory right
join Detective left

Mallory: I'm so worried about Felicia. I think that director was pressuring her. And Felix... I've never trusted him. He argues with her about money constantly. I've always thought he was bad for her.

label Questions
- Why did you call Felicia that night?
	Detective: Why did you call Felicia that night?
	Mallory: I-I call her sometimes. I wanted to hear her voice. Without everything else around her. Without people who needed something from her. Just her voice.
	jump Questions
- Were you jealous of her success?
	Detective: Were you jealous of her success?
	Mallory: Jealous? No. Not of the fame. Just of how easily she was loved for something I was never even allowed to try.
	jump Questions
- Did you meet her after the call?
	Detective: Did you meet her after the call?
	Mallory: She didn't want to go home. Not to that apartment where her letters to me would be lying around without a reply. (pause) If I had taken her somewhere... do you think I'd be sitting here?
	jump Questions
- Do you know where she is now?
	Detective: Do you know where she is now?
	Mallory (quietly): Maybe she wanted to run away. I don't know. (very quietly) But I miss her.
	jump Questions
- [Leave Interrogation]
	[end_timeline]
